# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js (App Router) project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package to project dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json`

### 2. Modified Files
- **web/app/layout.tsx**: Added Analytics component to root layout
  - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag, following Next.js App Router best practices

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Used the Next.js App Router setup pattern
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout file for site-wide tracking
- The component is added at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't block page rendering
- No environment variables or additional configuration required

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ Linter passed with no errors (`npm run lint`)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ All lock files updated

## Next Steps

To enable analytics in production:
1. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel dashboard
2. Click "Enable" for this project
3. Deploy these changes using `vercel deploy`
4. Analytics will automatically start collecting data once deployed

The analytics component will seamlessly integrate with Vercel's infrastructure upon deployment.
